shploingus.theme/339926f6b1b54ebb89810d4c6238d523
# The Popit shell scheme, which is the pinned baseline: ink ground, brass keyline, brass light for
# attention, warm paper for text, dim for meta. These are the inks F:/Documents/popit-shell draws
# with (its bar.css and style.css name #0f1113, #1c2125, #b08d57, #d9b779, #e6dbc2, #8b8778), and
# they are the same values openlock_pinned.css cuts the bar and the plate with. `renderer popit`
# asks the shell for the port's editor renderer; `form popit` is the geometry axis.
#
# The values below are roles, not CSS. The spine, tray, target rows, material swatches, tweak
# options and the shell's own windows all read them through tools/gen_shell_theme.py; no shell
# file declares a Popit hex.
theme	popit
	label	Popit
	source	popit-shell ui/bar.css and ui/style.css (ink, paper, brass, brass-lit, dim)
	body	#0F1113F2
	panel	#14171AF2
	title	#191D21F2
	meta	#0B0D0FF2
	border	#B08D57
	borderStrong	#D9B779
	ink	#E6DBC2
	muted	#8B8778
	accent	#B08D57
	alert	#7A2114
	alertBody	#FFE3DAF2
# The Popit palette reaches the game surfaces the shell frames. The HUD bar becomes the ink strip
# with the brass keyline; the shop takes the same ground with the brass accent border.
rule	.CitadelHudTopBar	background-color	role:body
rule	.CitadelHudTopBar	border-color	role:borderStrong
rule	.CitadelHudHeroShop	background-color	role:body
rule	.CitadelHudHeroShop	border-color	role:accent
